<title>USA: NY business loans rose $654 mln in Oct 30 week. [CORRECTED 00:30 GMT 8/11]</title>
<headline>NY business loans rose $654 mln in Oct 30 week. [CORRECTED 00:30 GMT 8/11]</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, rose $654 million to $42,829 million in the week ended October 30, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans rose $654 million to $43,079 million (Corrects from $42,079 million.)</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally rose $3,262 million (Corrects from billion) to $758,905 million.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
